  "body": "Three B-slice errors remain on current master after the merged #4004 16x8/8x16 correction. This PR fixes those remaining paths and adds synthetic regressions. It does **not** include or reimplement #4004.\n\n### Changes\n\n- **Bi-predicted 4x4 temporary luma destination:** `pDstY2` already includes the enclosing 8x8 offset. Adding that offset again targets the wrong region; use the current 4x4 subpartition offset, matching the main luma/chroma paths. A direct in-tree integer-pixel MC test checks all four enclosing regions, both reference predictions, and temporary/main-buffer canaries.\n- **B_SKIP internal deblocking strengths:** the zero-strength shortcut is valid for uniform P_SKIP, but B_SKIP uses direct prediction and can infer different references/motion inside the macroblock. Route it through the existing B-slice internal-strength calculation; preserve P_SKIP behavior.\n- **Temporal CAVLC reference cache:** temporal direct derivation writes `pDec->pRefIndex`, but the local `ref_idx_list` remains at its sentinel. The later motion-cache fill overwrites the derived reference state before adjacent non-direct `PredMv` calculations. Preserve each partition's derived references in that local list.\n\n### Validation\n\nFresh base: `1a0073f0322c8b74cbcb75ca1bb1c3d19d75538d`.\n\nOn macOS arm64, release scalar and AArch64 NEON builds, the optional `test/api/b_slice_regression.py` generates seven 40-frame 320x240 streams using FFmpeg 7.1/libx264. Both native console API modes (`DecodeFrameNoDelay` and legacy `DecodeFrame2`, with EOS drain) require exact output length and every Y/U/V byte to match the reference:\n\n| Case | Unmodified master maximum Y/U/V error | Patched scalar / NEON |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Spatial CABAC | 3 | 0 / 0 |\n| Spatial CAVLC, 4x4 transforms | 3 | 0 / 0 |\n| Temporal CABAC, 4x4 transforms | 3 | 0 / 0 |\n| Temporal CAVLC, 4x4 transforms | 207 | 0 / 0 |\n| Unweighted spatial CABAC | 3 | 0 / 0 |\n| Deblocking-disabled spatial CABAC control | 0 | 0 / 0 |\n| P-frame control | 0 | 0 / 0 |\n\nThe direct 4x4 regression passes with scalar/available native MC and fails when only its `rec_mb.cpp` correction is removed. The six tests in `DecUT_IdctResAddPred.cpp` pass in the focused test binary. `git diff --check` passes. Reproduction commands and limitations are in `test/api/b_slice_regression.md`; logs, fixture/reference hashes, executable identifiers and encoder parameters are generated by the script.\n\nEarlier Linux amd64 scalar/SSE/AVX2 runs on OpenH264 2.6.0 plus the exact #4004 backport and these corrections also matched retained synthetic spatial/temporal-CAVLC streams bit-for-bit in both API modes. Those support the fixes but are **not** a current-master Linux/full-suite claim. No full upstream vector suite or multi-threaded decoder conformance claim is made, and no expected vector hashes are changed. CAVLC with 8x8 transforms is outside these tests.\n\nAll new inputs are synthetic; no private footage/configuration is included. The developer-only script is BSD-2-Clause; FFmpeg/libx264 are optional test tools, not new build/runtime dependencies. Ready for maintainer review; feedback is welcome on whether to split the three related corrections or integrate the optional reference regression differently. GitHub CI has not reported checks yet; the full-suite and platform limitations above remain explicit.\n\nPrepared with Codex assistance.\n",
